WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.100
- Wellington, the capital
of New Zealand,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.960
is a city built on steep hills.

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.850
If you're a tourist,
you will probably stop by

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:08.220
the Wellington Cable Car
at some point,

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.200
which will pull you up from
the main shopping street

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:11.790
to the Botanic Gardens.

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.130
But if you're local, there
are more than a hundred

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.720
other cable cars in the city

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.630
and they are definitely
not for tourists.

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:21.150
- I purchased this house
at the end of 2020,

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:22.740
and we were just looking for a house.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.660
We weren't looking for a cable car house.

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.430
But this house just came with a cable car!

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:28.860
And we found out that
the previous owner

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.920
had some mobility issues,
and that's why she installed it.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.260
And I've been living
in this cable car house

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.910
for about two years.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.920
- Access Automation has
installed approximately

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.650
300 cable cars around New Zealand.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:43.350
Majority of those will be in Wellington
'cause that's our base,

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:45.570
but we also do installations
all around New Zealand

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.880
and all around the
Asia-Pacific for that matter.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.470
They've got lots of different names,

00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:51.090
hillside lift, incline lift,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.950
probably a more accurate description.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.070
The Australians call them inclinators,
which is a pretty cool name.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.630
- This isn't just about laziness

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:00.090
or having something swish
to raise your property prices.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.070
There are quite a few houses in this city

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.260
that are up on hills and only accessible

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.620
by long flights of stairs
or twisting, winding pathways,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.960
tucked behind other buildings
with no direct road.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.220
There are even some cable cars

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.760
that give access to several
different houses along one track.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.820
- Our larger cable cars are
for commercial installations,

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.230
for hotels and resorts.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.870
We're looking at 800kg,
10 passengers,

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.970
up to 200 meters in length.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.980
And some of them go on
almost vertical cliff faces.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:27.300
They're really spectacular.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.800
A typical small residential cable car
would carry two people,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.870
might run 15-20 meters,

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:37.440
be ideal for a retired couple
or just to get access to the home.

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.930
We still get a lot of
inquiries for new cable cars.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:42.720
A common inquiry is for
people wanting to develop

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:43.830
the back of their section.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.020
In the old days, they would
tend to build the houses

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.850
close to the access point to the road,

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:49.410
but with the cable car,
it gives the option

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.910
of opening up rear sections.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.040
There's road access to the front lot,

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:56.280
but if you've got a
30 or 40° gradient hill,

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.530
it's not practical for people to walk up

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:00.840
40 or 50 meters up a gradient like that.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.910
So that's where the cable
car comes into its own.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.250
The bar for safety's always going up.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.690
And that's one of our challenges,

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:09.390
is to meet the very high
requirements for safety

00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:11.460
without making them unaffordable.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.917
A small installation, you'd
probably be starting around

00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:16.440
200,000 New Zealand
dollars these days.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.910
There's significant investment.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.640
- So if you've got to
regularly lug bags of shopping

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.250
or anything else heavy
up 20 meters of stairs,

00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:25.560
or if you're older and
worrying that mobility issues

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:27.690
might mean you have to leave your home,

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:30.090
and you've got the money
to install one of these,

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:32.400
it is actually a reasonable approach.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.350
But cable cars like this aren't cheap.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:35.850
And like any other elevator,

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.180
they have to be regularly
inspected and certified.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:42.150
- Yeah, it was interesting moving in and,
never having owned a house before,

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:44.850
and suddenly the house
needs a warrant of fitness?

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.890
Which is something that
I'd never thought about!

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.590
It's something I've only
associated with cars in the past.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.290
- So cable cars are covered
by the Building Act.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:54.420
They're actually
considered to be buildings.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.600
They require an annual
warrant of fitness,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:01.230
and our company is registered
as an independent qualified party

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:03.720
to be able to inspect the cable cars.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:05.910
- These cable cars are
the same as elevators

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.410
in any other block of apartments.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:09.810
Just open to the elements,

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.163
and not quite vertical.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.550
- I think it's worth it if you're older.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:18.060
Like as a young, fairly, quite fit person,

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.100
I was a bit like, "Oh, okay,

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:23.700
"I guess I just have this
annual expense now!"

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.440
But it is fun for parties,

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.930
and everyone loves the cable car

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.600
and it is great when you're moving house.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.930
- I started Access Automation
pretty much 30 years ago.

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.240
And so we've been
designing and building them

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:37.590
and maintaining them for that long.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.720
It's been absolutely fabulous experience,

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.570
but I sort of feel like it's
time to pass the baton on now.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.780
That's something that requires new blood
to really let it flourish.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.540
It needs to be taken
beyond what I can do.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.090
I guess the most
satisfying part of this job

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:54.390
is the fact that we're doing something
that helps people.

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:56.910
We allow elderly people to
stay in their homes longer.

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:57.960
At the other end of the scale,

00:03:57.960 --> 00:03:59.640
young professional couples, we allow them

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:02.550
to develop properties
made on hillsides and sites

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:04.950
that wouldn't otherwise
be able to be built on.

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.360
So we're building a product

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.890
that it's got a human element to it.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.750
I guess that's why I've
been doing it for so long

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:10.700
and still enjoy it.

